<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Esigie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1504">1504</a>–1550</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Oba Esigie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Esigie was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oba-dynasty">Oba</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> who ruled during 1504–1550. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igala">Igala</a> and enlarged the Benin Empire, developed relations with the Portuguese, including trade and Christian missions, and his mother Idia became the first Iyoba (queen mother). His reign was a high point of Benin power and art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/esigie.jpg" alt="Esigie" width="320" height="356" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: of Bronze Casters Guild Igun Eronmwon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MARKK_C2897_Oba_with_two_dignitaries_DSC-1074_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
